<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Everglades</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Everglades are a vast subtropical wetland in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, formed by a slow-moving sheet of water flowing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-okeechobee">Lake Okeechobee</a> to Florida Bay. In the 19th century they became a refuge for Seminole bands who escaped removal to the west. Much of the area has been protected as Everglades National Park since 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/everglades.jpg" alt="Everglades" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Kraft · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Everglades_Pa-Hay-Oke_Swamp.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
